     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Hello,</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><br></span></font></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span>I&#39;m relatively new to R and GGIR, but was able to run this package on a few Geneactive .bin files. Thanks so much Vincent for creating this. </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span>I had a question - my summary report shoes movement and ”light\r\ndetected by light sensor” until about 3 am, which is when sleep/rest is\r\ndetected, but when we use the Excel macro provided by </span><span>Geneactive</span><span> to\r\nanalyze data, the bed time shows up as 22:09. </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span>I</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri;color:black\">’</span><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Calibri;font-size:12pt\">m not sure if this has happened\r\nbefore, but is it possible that my GGIR summary report timeline has shifted by a\r\ncouple of hours?</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Calibri;font-size:12pt\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Calibri;font-size:12pt\">Best,</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;word-break:normal\"><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Calibri;font-size:12pt\">Lydia</span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
    ]
